arsc reimplements published single-cell methods in Python so that their numerical output can be
checked against the reference software (see the *_PARITY.md files). Several modules are translations
of, or follow closely, the source code of the reference packages; each is listed below with the
original's licence. All of those licences allow inclusion in a GPL-3.0-or-later work. The methods
belong to their authors. If you use a method through arsc, please cite the original paper as well as
arsc.

Licence texts of the permissively licensed (MIT, BSD) originals are kept in LICENSES/, as their
licences require:
