Method credits
--------------
Normalisation, variable features, scaling, PCA, kNN/SNN graphs, WNN, FindMarkers/FindAllMarkers,
AverageExpression, CellCycleScoring, AddModuleScore (arsc.pp, arsc.neighbors, arsc.seurat_extra,
arsc.scores.add_module_score). Ported from Seurat 4.3.0 (R, MIT; LICENSES/Seurat-MIT.txt).
  - Satija R, et al. Spatial reconstruction of single-cell gene expression data. Nat Biotechnol (2015).
  - Stuart T, et al. Comprehensive integration of single-cell data. Cell (2019).
  - Hao Y, et al. Integrated analysis of multimodal single-cell data. Cell (2021).
  - Hao Y, et al. Dictionary learning for integrative, multimodal and scalable single-cell analysis.
    Nat Biotechnol (2024).
  - Cell-cycle gene lists: Tirosh I, et al. Science (2016).

Harmony integration (arsc.run_harmony, arsc.harmony). Translated from harmony 1.2.0 (R/C++, GPL-3).
  - Korsunsky I, et al. Fast, sensitive and accurate integration of single-cell data with Harmony.
    Nat Methods (2019).

Symphony reference mapping (arsc.symphony). Translated from symphony 0.1.1 (R/C++, GPL (>= 3); authors
Joyce Kang, Ilya Korsunsky, Soumya Raychaudhuri): reference compression, query projection, soft clustering, the
mixture-of-experts query correction, kNN label transfer and the per-cell mapping metric.
  - Kang JB, et al. Efficient and precise single-cell reference atlas mapping with Symphony.
    Nat Commun 12, 5890 (2021).

Fast Wilcoxon / AUC markers (arsc.wilcoxauc). Follows presto 1.0.0 (R, GPL-3).
  - Korsunsky I, Nathan A, Millard N, Raychaudhuri S. Presto scales Wilcoxon and auROC analyses to
    millions of observations. bioRxiv (2019).

UCell signature scores (arsc.score_ucell). Follows UCell 2.6.2 (R, GPL-3).
  - Andreatta M, Carmona SJ. UCell: Robust and scalable single-cell gene signature scoring.
    Comput Struct Biotechnol J (2021).

Pseudobulk differential expression (arsc.de).
  - DESeq2: Love MI, Huber W, Anders S. Genome Biol (2014). arsc calls pydeseq2 (MIT), an independent
    Python implementation, as an optional dependency; the parametric dispersion-trend fit in
    arsc.de follows DESeq2 1.42.1 parametricDispersionFit (R, LGPL (>= 3)).
  - limma: Ritchie ME, et al. Nucleic Acids Res (2015). voom: Law CW, et al. Genome Biol (2014).
    arsc.de.voom, duplicate_correlation, fitFDist/eBayes and gls are translated from limma 3.58.1
    (R, GPL (>= 2)); the duplicateCorrelation REML model follows statmod 1.5.0 mixedModel2Fit
    (R, GPL-2 | GPL-3).
  - edgeR: Robinson MD, McCarthy DJ, Smyth GK. Bioinformatics (2010). TMM normalisation:
    Robinson MD, Oshlack A. Genome Biol (2010). arsc.de.tmm_factors and filter_by_expr are
    translated from edgeR 4.0.16 (R, GPL (>= 2)).
  - fgsea: Korotkevich G, et al. Fast gene set enrichment analysis. bioRxiv (2021). arsc.de.fgsea
    ports fgsea 1.28.0 (R, MIT; LICENSES/fgsea-MIT.txt).

scanpy-parity functions (arsc.scanpy_extra). Ported from scanpy 1.11 (BSD-3-Clause;
LICENSES/scanpy-BSD-3-Clause.txt).
  - Wolf FA, Angerer P, Theis FJ. SCANPY: large-scale single-cell gene expression data analysis.
    Genome Biol (2018).
  - Leiden: Traag VA, Waltman L, van Eck NJ. From Louvain to Leiden. Sci Rep (2019).
  - UMAP: McInnes L, Healy J, Melville J. arXiv (2018).
  - Diffusion pseudotime: Haghverdi L, et al. Nat Methods (2016).
  - Palantir diffusion maps: Setty M, et al. Nat Biotechnol (2019). scanpy_extra.palantir_diffusion_maps,
    palantir_multiscale_space and magic_impute follow palantir 1.4.5 (palantir.utils). Palantir is MIT
    (PyPI metadata for 1.4.5 and the repository LICENSE, checked 2026-10-15); text in LICENSES/.
  - MAGIC imputation: van Dijk D, et al. Cell (2018).

Clonal analysis (arsc.clones, arsc.clonotrace).
  - STARTRAC indices: Zhang L, et al. Lineage tracking reveals dynamic relationships of T cells in
    colorectal cancer. Nature (2018).
  - Cyclone clone-trajectory clustering: ports cyclone_find_trajectories() from the analysis
    script clone_trajectory_util.R of the Cancer Cell 2024 publication, written by the arsc
    author (jiwen90), who licenses this port under arsc's licence; see the clones.cyclone docstring and CLONES_PARITY.md.
  - STARTRAC: reimplemented from the paper's formulas (the Startrac R package is not a source).
  - CloneTrace: Fu Y, et al. Deciphering Cell Fate and Clonal Dynamics via Integrative Single-Cell
    Lineage Modeling. bioRxiv 2025.09.01.673503. arsc.clonotrace ports the Clonotrace R package
    v1.2.1 (MIT; LICENSES/Clonotrace-MIT.txt).

R-compatible components.
  - arsc._loess reproduces R's stats::loess default fit: the netlib dloess code of Cleveland,
    Grosse and Shyu (AT&T permissive notice) as modified in R's stats package (R: GPL-2 | GPL-3).
  - arsc._rrng reproduces R's default random number generator (Mersenne Twister, Matsumoto and
    Nishimura 1998; R's seeding and inversion scheme from R's RNG.c, GPL (>= 2)) so that seeded R
    functions can be matched.
  - arsc.stats: the exact signed-rank counts follow R's stats package (GPL-2 | GPL-3); glmm_prop
    is its own Laplace implementation that follows lme4 1.1-35 conventions (GPL (>= 2)).

Third-party optional dependencies
---------------------------------
arsc does not bundle third-party packages. Some optional extras install packages under other
licences:
  - leidenalg (GPL-3.0-or-later) and python-igraph (GPL-2.0-or-later), in the "graph" extra,
    used by arsc.cluster and arsc.scanpy_extra.leiden.
  - pydeseq2 (MIT), statsmodels (BSD-3-Clause), patsy (BSD-2-Clause), in the "stats" extra.
  - POT (MIT), in the "clonotrace" extra.
The optional R bridge (arsc/R/export_seurat.R) runs under the user's own R installation with
SeuratObject (MIT) and, optionally, qs.

Licence compatibility of the originals with GPL-3.0-or-later
-------------------------------------------------------------
  - GPL-3 (harmony, presto, UCell), GPL (>= 2) (limma, edgeR, lme4, R's RNG.c), GPL-2 | GPL-3 (R
    stats, statmod) and LGPL (>= 3) (DESeq2): compatible.
  - MIT (Seurat, fgsea, Clonotrace, palantir) and BSD-3-Clause (scanpy): compatible; their notices are kept in
    LICENSES/.
  - A GPL-2.0-only original would NOT be compatible with GPL-3.0-or-later; none is known to be ported.
